  ('lesson', 'identity', 'Who you are beyond your roles', 'Your roles (parent, partner, professional, friend) describe what you do for others. Your identity is the person underneath: your values, your preferences, what moves you and what you stand for. When roles change, people who know only their roles often feel lost. Knowing your identity gives you a steady center that travels with you.', 'Someone who has always been ''the dependable one'' may realize, after a career change, that they also love creativity and play: parts of themselves they had set aside.', 'Which of your roles takes up the most space in how you describe yourself? What would remain if that role changed?', 'Write five sentences that begin with ''I am someone who...'' without mentioning a job title or relationship.', null, 'foundations-of-becoming', 1, 'peace', 'draft'),
  ('lesson', 'self-love', 'Self-love as daily practice', 'Self-love is not a feeling you wait for; it is a set of choices. It shows up in how you speak to yourself, the promises you keep to yourself, and the rest and care you allow yourself. It is not selfishness: people who treat themselves with respect are better able to offer it to others.', 'After a mistake at work, one person spends the evening criticizing themselves; another acknowledges the mistake, plans one improvement and then rests. Both care about doing well; only one is practicing self-love.', 'How do you speak to yourself after a mistake? Would you speak to a friend that way?', 'Choose one small promise to keep to yourself every day this week, and notice how it feels to keep it.', null, 'foundations-of-becoming', 2, 'peace', 'draft'),
  ('lesson', 'emotional-intelligence', 'Naming what you feel', 'Emotional intelligence begins with noticing and naming emotions accurately. ''I feel bad'' is hard to work with; ''I feel disappointed and a little embarrassed'' points toward what you need. Naming a feeling also tends to soften its intensity, giving you more choice in how you respond.', 'Instead of snapping at a partner after a long day, someone pauses and recognizes: ''I''m not angry at you. I''m exhausted and feel unappreciated at work.''', 'Which emotions are easiest for you to name? Which do you tend to skip over?', 'Three times today, pause and name your feeling with two words: one for the emotion and one for its intensity.', null, 'foundations-of-becoming', 3, 'peace', 'draft'),
  ('lesson', 'communication', 'Listening to understand', 'Most conversations go wrong not because of what is said but because of how we listen. Listening to understand means staying curious, asking questions and reflecting back what you heard before offering your view. People who feel heard become more open to hearing you.', 'Before replying in a disagreement, someone says, ''So what I''m hearing is that you felt left out of the decision. Is that right?'' The tension drops immediately.', 'In your conversations this week, were you listening to understand, or waiting to reply?', 'In one conversation today, summarize what the other person said before you share your own view.', null, 'foundations-of-becoming', 4, 'peace', 'draft'),
  ('lesson', 'boundaries', 'Boundaries that protect connection', 'A boundary is a clear statement of what you will and will not do, not a demand that others change. Healthy boundaries protect your energy and, surprisingly, strengthen relationships: people know where they stand with you, and resentment has less room to grow.', 'Rather than silently resenting late-night work messages, someone says, ''I answer messages until 7 pm; anything after that I''ll handle first thing in the morning.''', 'Where do you feel resentment building? Resentment often marks a boundary that hasn''t been spoken.', 'Write one boundary you need, phrased as what you will do: ''I will...'' rather than ''You must...''', null, 'foundations-of-becoming', 5, 'peace', 'draft'),
  ('lesson', 'relationships', 'What healthy connection looks like', 'Healthy relationships, whether friendships, partnerships or professional connections, share a few qualities: mutual respect, honesty, reliability and room for each person to grow. They are not free of conflict; they handle conflict with care. Knowing these qualities helps you recognize them, and offer them.', 'Two friends disagree about a plan. Instead of withdrawing, one says, ''I value our friendship more than being right about this. Can we find something that works for both of us?''', 'Which of your relationships leaves you feeling more like yourself? What do they have in common?', 'Send a short, genuine note of appreciation to someone who adds value to your life.', null, 'foundations-of-becoming', 6, 'peace', 'draft'),
  ('lesson', 'work-ethic', 'Consistency over intensity', 'Lasting results rarely come from bursts of effort; they come from showing up consistently. A strong work ethic is less about long hours and more about reliability: doing what you said you would, when you said you would, with care.', 'Someone building a business commits to thirty focused minutes every morning rather than occasional all-night sessions, and finds more progress after a month.', 'Where in your life would steady, small effort make the biggest difference?', 'Choose one task and do it for fifteen focused minutes every day this week.', null, 'foundations-of-becoming', 7, 'peace', 'draft'),
  ('lesson', 'financial-mindset', 'Your relationship with money', 'How you think and feel about money shapes your decisions as much as how much you have. Beliefs formed early (''money is always tight'', ''talking about money is rude'') can quietly guide adult choices. Understanding your money story is the first step to writing a healthier one. This lesson is educational, not financial advice.', 'Someone notices they feel anxious checking their account, rooted in childhood worries. Naming that pattern helps them build a calm weekly money check-in.', 'What did you learn about money growing up? Which of those beliefs still serve you?', 'Write down three beliefs you hold about money, and mark each one: helpful, unhelpful or unsure.', null, 'foundations-of-becoming', 8, 'peace', 'draft'),
  ('lesson', 'values', 'Living by your values', 'Values are what matter most to you: honesty, family, freedom, creativity, faith, growth. When your choices align with your values, life feels meaningful even when it is hard. When they don''t, even success can feel empty.', 'Someone who values family declines a promotion that would require constant travel, and feels peace instead of regret.', 'Name your top three values. Where did your time go this week, and does it reflect them?', 'Look at your calendar for the coming week and move one thing to better reflect a top value.', null, 'foundations-of-becoming', 9, 'peace', 'draft'),
  ('lesson', 'confidence', 'Confidence is built, not found', 'Confidence is not the absence of doubt; it is trust in your ability to handle what comes. It grows from evidence: each time you do something difficult, keep a commitment, or recover from a setback, you add to that evidence.', 'Someone nervous about speaking up in meetings starts by asking one question per meeting. Within weeks, sharing ideas feels natural.', 'What evidence do you already have that you can handle hard things?', 'Do one small thing today that feels slightly outside your comfort zone, and write down how it went.', null, 'foundations-of-becoming', 10, 'peace', 'draft'),
  ('lesson', 'intentional-living', 'Choosing on purpose', 'Intentional living means making choices on purpose rather than by default: how you spend your time, who you spend it with and what you give your attention to. It does not require a perfect plan, only regular pauses to ask whether your days reflect what you want.', 'Someone notices they spend evenings scrolling out of habit and replaces one evening a week with a walk and a call to a friend.', 'If your next year looked exactly like your last month, would you be satisfied?', 'At the end of today, write one thing you did on purpose and one thing you did by default.', null, 'foundations-of-becoming', 11, 'peace', 'draft'),
  ('scenario', 'communication', 'A friend cancels plans at the last minute for the third time.', 'How would you most likely respond?', null, null, null, '[{"key": "a", "label": "Tell them honestly how it affected me and ask what''s going on", "insight": "You tend to address things directly and kindly.", "signals": ["communication:direct", "explore:friendship"]}, {"key": "b", "label": "Say it''s fine, but feel hurt and pull back a little", "insight": "You may protect peace at the cost of your own needs.", "signals": ["communication:reserved", "explore:friendship"]}, {"key": "c", "label": "Give them space and check in later", "insight": "You value patience and giving others room.", "signals": ["communication:reflective", "explore:friendship"]}]'::jsonb, null, null, 'peace', 'draft'),
  ('scenario', 'communication', 'You and a colleague disagree about how to approach an important project.', 'What feels most natural to you?', null, null, null, '[{"key": "a", "label": "Talk it through right away to find common ground", "insight": "You prefer resolving disagreements openly and promptly.", "signals": ["conflict:address", "explore:business"]}, {"key": "b", "label": "Take time to think, then suggest a solution in writing", "insight": "You prefer reflection before discussion.", "signals": ["conflict:reflect", "explore:business"]}, {"key": "c", "label": "Ask a third person to help weigh both ideas", "insight": "You value fairness and outside perspective.", "signals": ["conflict:mediate", "explore:business"]}]'::jsonb, null, null, 'peace', 'draft'),
  ('scenario', 'relationships', 'You have a free Saturday evening.', 'Which sounds most restoring?', null, null, null, '[{"key": "a", "label": "Dinner with one or two close friends", "insight": "You recharge through deep, small-group connection.", "signals": ["social:small-group", "explore:friendship"]}, {"key": "b", "label": "A lively event where you can meet new people", "insight": "You draw energy from new people and lively settings.", "signals": ["social:large-group", "explore:social"]}, {"key": "c", "label": "A quiet evening for yourself", "insight": "You recharge through solitude and reflection.", "signals": ["social:solitude", "explore:growth"]}, {"key": "d", "label": "Planning a weekend trip", "insight": "Adventure and new places restore you.", "signals": ["social:adventure", "explore:travel"]}]'::jsonb, null, null, 'peace', 'draft'),
  ('scenario', 'work-ethic', 'You''re starting a new project with a deadline in a month.', 'How do you like to work?', null, null, null, '[{"key": "a", "label": "Build a detailed plan first, then follow it", "insight": "You value structure and predictability.", "signals": ["work:structured", "explore:business"]}, {"key": "b", "label": "Start quickly and adjust as I learn", "insight": "You value momentum and flexibility.", "signals": ["work:flexible", "explore:business"]}, {"key": "c", "label": "Bring others in early to shape it together", "insight": "You value collaboration and shared ownership.", "signals": ["work:collaborative", "explore:business"]}]'::jsonb, null, null, 'peace', 'draft'),
  ('scenario', 'relationships', 'A new acquaintance is very outspoken and quick to share strong opinions.', 'How do you tend to feel?', null, null, null, '[{"key": "a", "label": "Energized: I enjoy a spirited conversation", "insight": "You enjoy directness and debate.", "signals": ["interaction:enjoys-directness"]}, {"key": "b", "label": "Comfortable, as long as there''s mutual respect", "insight": "You adapt well to different styles when respect is present.", "signals": ["interaction:adaptive"]}, {"key": "c", "label": "Drained: I prefer calmer conversations", "insight": "You feel most at ease with gentle, measured communication.", "signals": ["interaction:prefers-gentle"]}]'::jsonb, null, null, 'peace', 'draft'),
  ('scenario', 'relationships', 'You imagine a meaningful connection a year from now.', 'Which feels most important to you right now?', null, null, null, '[{"key": "a", "label": "A romantic partnership built on shared values", "insight": "", "signals": ["explore:singles"]}, {"key": "b", "label": "Deepening the relationship I''m already in", "insight": "", "signals": ["explore:couples"]}, {"key": "c", "label": "New friendships with people who share my interests", "insight": "", "signals": ["explore:friendship"]}, {"key": "d", "label": "Professional relationships that help my work grow", "insight": "", "signals": ["explore:business"]}]'::jsonb, null, null, 'peace', 'draft'),
  ('scenario', 'values', 'You''re offered an opportunity that pays well but conflicts with something you value.', 'What do you do?', null, null, null, '[{"key": "a", "label": "Decline: alignment matters more to me", "insight": "Your values guide your decisions strongly.", "signals": ["values:alignment-first"]}, {"key": "b", "label": "Look for a way to make it fit my values", "insight": "You look for creative solutions that honor your values.", "signals": ["values:creative"]}, {"key": "c", "label": "Take it for now and revisit later", "insight": "You balance practical needs with long-term values.", "signals": ["values:pragmatic"]}]'::jsonb, null, null, 'peace', 'draft'),
  ('scenario', 'intentional-living', 'Picture your ideal next twelve months.', 'What would make them feel full?', null, null, null, '[{"key": "a", "label": "Growing a business or career I''m proud of", "insight": "", "signals": ["explore:business", "ambition:career"]}, {"key": "b", "label": "Travel and new experiences", "insight": "", "signals": ["explore:travel", "lifestyle:adventure"]}, {"key": "c", "label": "Strong friendships and community", "insight": "", "signals": ["explore:friendship", "explore:social"]}, {"key": "d", "label": "Personal growth and inner peace", "insight": "", "signals": ["explore:growth", "explore:wellness"]}]'::jsonb, null, null, 'peace', 'draft'),
  ('scenario', 'intentional-living', 'You want to learn something new.', 'How do you prefer to learn?', null, null, null, '[{"key": "a", "label": "Live sessions where I can ask questions", "insight": "", "signals": ["learning:live", "explore:webinars"]}, {"key": "b", "label": "Reading and reflecting on my own", "insight": "", "signals": ["learning:self-paced"]}, {"key": "c", "label": "Learning alongside a group", "insight": "", "signals": ["learning:group", "explore:social"]}]'::jsonb, null, null, 'peace', 'draft'),
  ('scenario', 'communication', 'Someone gives you feedback you didn''t expect.', 'What is your first instinct?', null, null, null, '[{"key": "a", "label": "Ask questions to understand it fully", "insight": "You meet feedback with curiosity.", "signals": ["communication:curious"]}, {"key": "b", "label": "Take time alone to process it", "insight": "You prefer reflection before responding.", "signals": ["communication:reflective"]}, {"key": "c", "label": "Explain my side so they understand", "insight": "You value being understood and clear.", "signals": ["communication:direct"]}]'::jsonb, null, null, 'peace', 'draft'),
